## Result

`/work/submission.csv` is written and verified against all acceptance criteria:

| Check | Result |
|-------|--------|
| Columns identical to `sample_submission.csv` (`id`, `satisfaction`) | PASS |
| Ids identical and in same order (299,844 rows) | PASS |
| `satisfaction` values are probabilities in [0,1], no NaNs | PASS (range 0.003–0.989, 0 nulls) |
| Local stratified 5-fold LightGBM CV ROC AUC | 0.9588 (target >0.90) |

## What I did

1. **Explored data**: train 699,635 × 23, test 299,844 × 22; target `satisfaction` is boolean (44% positive); only missing values: 292 in `Arrival Delay in Minutes`.
2. **Preprocessing**: filled missing arrival delays with departure delay then median; ratings are 1–5 Likert; casted `Gender`, `Customer Type`, `Type of Travel`, `Class` as LightGBM native categoricals; dropped `id`.
3. **Model**: LightGBM (4.6.0, callbacks-based early stopping), stratified 5-fold CV with ROC AUC, `n_estimators=4000`, `lr=0.03`, `num_leaves=63`, `subsample/colsample=0.8`, `reg_lambda=2`. Fold AUCs: 0.9590, 0.9577, 0.9595, 0.9589, 0.9592 → mean **0.9588**.
4. **Tried one improvement**: added total delay, avg/min service rating, and delay×business-class interaction features — CV was unchanged (0.9588), so no added complexity.
5. **Final**: averaged the 5 fold probability predictions on the test set, clipped to [0,1], wrote `/work/submission.csv`.

No internet was used; only pandas/numpy/lightgbm/sklearn. Total runtime well under the 12-minute limit. Note: I could not create `.harness/` state files (the directory is owned by uid 1001 without write access for the agent user), so protocol state lives only in this report.
